{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Yesterday morning we crossed the beautiful, broad, stately Scheldt into the great Antwerp, again with 60–70,000 inhabitants; Ghent has just as many. In these cities one must see the churches! In Antwerp the world-famous Cathedral—in the nave of it, as in the unfinished cathedral in Cologne, 3 rows of columns on each side; how spacious and free one wanders about in it!—The spaces are not blocked up with church pews and benches, there is no bench in it, everything free, but there stands a pile of 100 chairs stacked up, of which each person who comes has one given to them, carries it from one altar to another;—here a small group, there a crowd, always changing, coming and going. The Hague, 9th Oct. Evening."}}],"created":1795220643,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":178,"prompt_tokens":270,"total_tokens":448,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-tJxKhZNWjGF2lmbEQbygfxmmrUR0q2Wl","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":270,"prompt_ms":397.792,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.4733037037037036,"prompt_per_second":678.7466816828896,"predicted_n":178,"predicted_ms":4206.514,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.76561581920904,"predicted_per_second":42.07759679392485}}